    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0453" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 259.</note>
                <head>Mr. Thornton to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 2, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 31st ultimo relative to the exception which you took to the
                    wording of the Canadian order in council of the 8th of January last, relative to
                    the fisheries in the neighborhood of Canada.</p>
                <p>I am inclined to think that you are right in supposing that the limit of Canada
                    extends as far east as Ance Sablon on the coast of Labrador, and that the
                    Magdalen Islands are comprised within it, for I am not aware that any change has
                    been made since the act of Parliament of 1825 quoted in your note.</p>
                <p>I have, however, transmitted a copy of your, note to the Governor General of
                    Canada, and shall not fail to acquaint you with the nature of his answer.</p>
            </div>
